---
import StudioNavigation from './StudioNavigation.astro';
import ResearchProjectFrame from './ResearchProjectFrame.astro';
import '../styles/tokens.css';
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/research-programs.css';
const privateLocalReview = import.meta.env.MODE === 'local-review';
const routes=[
 ['Methods','/workbench/','Practice, technique sheets, applied prompts, and four independent case-report tabs.'],
 ['Dossier','/dossier/','A complete Ember Circuit character sheet with eight hypothetical attributes, feats, dispositions, and loadout.'],
 ['Questions','/research/','A selectable inquiry ledger, four tensions, and a compact worked question guide.'],
 ['Programs','/programs/','Seven focused studies using HCAN’s shared project frame. Longer source collections remain expandable.'],
 ['Typed Context for Real Work','/journal/typed-context-for-real-work/','Centered, single-column reading surface with expandable contents.'],
 ['Knowledge Representation Without a Black Box','/journal/knowledge-representation-without-a-black-box/','Centered, single-column reading surface with expandable contents.'],
 ['TCCP','/programs/tccp/','Eight-section research disposition.'],['EKRP','/programs/ekrp/','Eight-section research disposition.'],
 ['Core32','/programs/core32/','Eight-section evaluation-research disposition.'],['ESS','/programs/ess/','Eight-section standards-program disposition.'],
 ['HCAN','/hcan/','Reference project frame with grammar, examples, evaluation context, and limits.'],
 ['Exocore','/review/exocore/','System study using the shared project frame.'],['Ember Circuit','/review/ember-circuit/','Design-system study using the shared project frame.'],
 ['Studio','/','Hearth and Code front door.'],['Research','/research/','Research directory and cross-references.'],
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><title>Modular Surface Review · Hearth &amp; Code</title></head><body>
<StudioNavigation current="research" disposition="Local review / modular reconciliation · 2 October 2026" />
<main id="page-main"><ResearchProjectFrame eyebrow="Local review / 2 October 2026" title="A smaller surface. More ways into the work." summary="Review the modular reconciliation pass: repaired article reading fields, interactive Methods layers, a new character sheet, focused Research Program studies, and consistent Questions typography." status="Review candidate · goal active" facts={[{label:'Scope',value:'Local landing candidate'},{label:'Layout checks',value:'1440 / 390 / 320 pixels'},{label:'Interactions',value:'Tabs, keyboard, selectors, section links'},{label:'Release',value:'No production publication'}]} sections={[{id:'updated-surfaces',label:'Updated surfaces'},{id:'review-boundaries',label:'Limits & next review'}]} returnHref="/" returnLabel="Return to Studio">
<section class="program-directory-grid" id="updated-surfaces" aria-label="Updated review surfaces">{routes.map(([title,href,note])=><a href={href}><h2>{title}</h2><p>{note}</p><span>Review surface →</span></a>)}</section>
<section class="program-study-related" id="review-boundaries"><h2>Evidence and remaining boundaries</h2><p>All 25 browser checks passed, including audience journeys, visible keyboard focus, method-sheet deep links, article families, and source-status boundaries. An additional scoped check exercised all seven program frames, both repaired articles, Methods, Questions, and Dossier at 1440, 390, and 320 pixels, including arrow-key tab navigation and legacy anchors, with no client runtime errors. These checks establish the specified layout and interactions; human review of clarity and design remains open.</p><p>The 128 technique demonstrations retain their exact prompt-bound receipts: 113 validated records and 15 review holds. No new model evaluations were run for this layout pass.</p><p>{privateLocalReview ? "Finalized for private local review: the separate 512-template catalog is available under Methods → Prompt Catalog → Task templates, with search, declared inputs, local previews, and provenance. Its data stays outside the public repository and ordinary build." : "The separate internal 512-template catalog stays private. This build contains the 128 applied technique prompts; the private local review provides the separate task-template browser."}</p><p>Research dispositions remain public explanatory projections. Hypothetical character-sheet scores are design values. Fieldcraft’s Lean-style proof claims remain unverified. Publication and Git release remain separate actions.</p></section>
</ResearchProjectFrame></main></body></html>
